l is appropriate."}]}]},{"heading":"Hardware-Software Co-Design","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This is central to the target career."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how to divide system functionality between:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hardware"},{"text":"↕"},{"text":"Firmware"},{"text":"↕"},{"text":"Drivers"},{"text":"↕"},{"text":"Middleware"},{"text":"↕"},{"text":"Application Software"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Important considerations:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Performance"},{"text":"Power consumption"},{"text":"Latency"},{"text":"Memory"},{"text":"Reliability"},{"text":"Cost"},{"text":"Security"},{"text":"Maintainability"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Example:"},{"type":"p","text":"A sensor-processing task might be moved from software to dedicated hardware when latency requirements cannot be achieved efficiently through software alone."}]},{"heading":"Debugging & Testing","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Integration engineers spend significant time identifying problems that occur between hardware and software."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"h","text":"Software Debugging"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"GDB"},{"text":"Logging"},{"text":"Unit testing"},{"text":"Static analysis"},{"text":"Profiling"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Hardware Debugging"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Multimeter"},{"text":"Oscilloscope"},{"text":"Logic analyzer"},{"text":"JTAG/SWD"},{"text":"Serial console"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Integration Testing"},{"type":"flow","items":["Hardware Test","Firmware Test","Driver Test","Subsystem Test","System Integration Test","Validation"]}]},{"heading":"PCB & Hardware Design Fundamentals","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The engineer does not necessarily need to become a PCB designer, but should understand the basics."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Schematic reading"},{"text":"PCB layout concepts"},{"text":"Component selection"},{"text":"Signal integrity fundamentals"},